{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyZ2RfpGXHHN8cHLmyH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0151ARjB5sJk3iTQ2KQU83YL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-vG8Hwi; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import time\\n\",\"import time\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace('\"score\": similarity(story, other)})','\"score\": Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))})')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_publish.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\n\nif __name__''','''\n    def test_second_publish_with_similar_stories(self):\n        table = FakeTable()\n        app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"first-story\", \"title\": \"A\", \"tags\": [\"cron\", \"linux\"], \"body\": \"two crontabs ran\"})\n        stored = app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"second-story\", \"title\": \"B\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"], \"body\": \"one crontab ran\"})\n        self.assertEqual(stored[\"similar\"][0][\"slug\"], \"first-story\")\n        self.assertEqual(table.scan()[\"Count\"], 2)\n\n\nif __name__''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nopen('ANSWER.md','w').write('''# Second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n`related()` in `src/app.py` puts a Python `float` (`score`, from `similarity()`) into the item's `similar` list.\nboto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats (`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`),\nso `put_item` fails and the handler returns 500.\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty: `similar` was `[]`, so there were no floats.\nEvery publish after that has at least one existing story, so it carries a float score and fails.\nThe old test only published one story into an empty table, so it never hit this.\n\n## Fix\n- `related()` now stores `Decimal(str(score))` (via `str` so the stored value is the rounded 4-digit number, not a binary float expansion).\n- Added `test_second_publish_with_similar_stories`, which publishes two stories. The fake table rejects floats the way boto3 does, so a float would fail this test.\n\n## Not changed\n`publish()` reads existing stories with a single `scan`, which returns at most 1 MB per call.\nOnce the library is larger than that, `similar` will only be computed from part of it.\n''')\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover tests 2>&1 | tail -4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_read_input_tokens":21302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1996a78e-7a8a-492a-b4da-862d789fe53c","uuid":"6ff9662c-8ba8-494a-a01c-24b3ed16bc8a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:45:52.788Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyZ294GQhhtvNesEgzG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0151ARjB5sJk3iTQ2KQU83YL":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-vG8Hwi; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import time\\n\",\"import time\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace('\"score\": similarity(story, other)})','\"score\": Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))})')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_publish.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\n\nif __name__''','''\n    def test_second_publish_with_similar_stories(self):\n        table = FakeTable()\n        app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"first-story\", \"title\": \"A\", \"tags\": [\"cron\", \"linux\"], \"body\": \"two crontabs ran\"})\n        stored = app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"second-story\", \"title\": \"B\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"], \"body\": \"one crontab ran\"})\n        self.assertEqual(stored[\"similar\"][0][\"slug\"], \"first-story\")\n        self.assertEqual(table.scan()[\"Count\"], 2)\n\n\nif __name__''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nopen('ANSWER.md','w').write('''# Second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n`related()` in `src/app.py` puts a Python `float` (`score`, from `similarity()`) into the item's `similar` list.\nboto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats (`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`),\nso `put_item` fails and the handler returns 500.\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty: `similar` was `[]`, so there were no floats.\nEvery publish after that has at least one existing story, so it carries a float score and fails.\nThe old test only published one story into an empty table, so it never hit this.\n\n## Fix\n- `related()` now stores `Decimal(str(score))` (via `str` so the stored value is the rounded 4-digit number, not a binary float expansion).\n- Added `test_second_publish_with_similar_stories`, which publishes two stories. The fake table rejects floats the way boto3 does, so a float would fail this test.\n\n## Not changed\n`publish()` reads existing stories with a single `scan`, which returns at most 1 MB per call.\nOnce the library is larger than that, `similar` will only be computed from part of it.\n''')\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover tests 2>&1 | tail -4"}}}
