{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyZdMNh5bAZuYoy7LQu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish fails because the `score` values in `similar` are Python floats, and boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats. The log shows `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`\n\nThe first publish worked only because the table was empty, so `similar` was an empty list. Every later publish has existing stories to compare against, so it carries float scores and `put_item` fails with a 500.\n\n**Fix:** `related()` in `src/app.py` now stores each score as `Decimal(str(score))`. Going through `str` keeps the rounded 4-digit value instead of a long binary-float expansion.\n\n**Regression test:** I added `test_second_publish_with_similar_stories`, which publishes two stories in a row. The fake table rejects floats the way boto3 does, so reintroducing a float would fail the test. Both tests pass. The old test only published one story into an empty table, which is why it missed this.\n\nI didn't change one related issue: `publish()` reads existing stories with a single `scan`, which returns at most 1 MB per call. Once the library outgrows that, `similar` will be computed from only part of it. I noted this in `ANSWER.md`, along with the cause and the fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":24075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084},"output_tokens":393,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1996a78e-7a8a-492a-b4da-862d789fe53c","uuid":"90877740-f089-4407-9352-bdbe6f0b1411","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:45:56.517Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyZd5zriT2H4gtKPAyp"}
